---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import PageHead from '../components/PageHead.astro';
import { site } from '../../site.config.mjs';
const p = site.privacy;
// POL-54 §B5 pide que la tabla salga de un escaneo del sitio real y no de la
// memoria de nadie: "A cookie policy that does not match what the site sets
// is itself a compliance failure". El escaneo de este sitio devuelve cero
// cookies, cero almacenamiento y cero peticiones a terceros, así que la tabla
// no existe y lo que se publica es esa ausencia.
---
<Base title="Cookies"
      description="Regent Orthodontics' cookie policy: this website sets no cookies, stores nothing on your device and loads nothing from third parties.">
  <PageHead eyebrow="Cookies"
            title="This site does not set any."
            lede="Most cookie policies explain a banner. This one explains why there is not one." />

  <section>
    <div class="wrap prose narrow">
      {p.confirmed === false && (
        <p class="warnbar"><span>This page reproduces POL-54, the practice's cookie policy. It takes
          effect when the practice opens to patients, which cannot happen until RQIA has granted
          registration.</span></p>
      )}

      <div class="blk">
        <h2>What we found when we checked</h2>
        <p>UK cookie law changed on 5 February 2026, when the Data (Use and Access) Act 2025
          replaced the old "strictly necessary" exception with a wider set of exceptions. Under the
          new rules a site that carries no advertising and no third-party tracking may need no
          consent banner at all. This is one of those sites.</p>
        <ul class="ticks">
          <li><span>No cookies of any kind, first-party or third-party</span></li>
          <li><span>Nothing kept in local storage or session storage on your device</span></li>
          <li><span>No analytics, no advertising, no pixels, no tags and no fingerprinting</span></li>
          <li><span>No embedded maps, videos, chat widgets or social media feeds — the map on our
            pages is a plain image generated here, not a service loaded from somewhere else</span></li>
          <li><span>No requests to any other website when you load a page. The typefaces are
            served from this site rather than from a font service, so visiting does not tell
            anyone else you were here</span></li>
        </ul>

        {/* La lista decía "no requests to any other website at all", y ese "at all" era
             absoluto: dejaba de ser cierto en cuanto alguien pulsa Send. Acotarlo a la carga
             de página lo vuelve exacto, pero callar la excepción en una página que presume de
             no hacer teatro desentonaba. Se declara. */}
        <p class="exception">The one exception is the enquiry form. When you press Send — and
          only then — what you have typed is sent to the service that passes it to us. Nothing
          is stored on your device either way.</p>
        <p>Because nothing is set, there is nothing to consent to and nothing to refuse. That is
          also why there is no cookie banner: a banner asking permission for something that does
          not exist would be theatre.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="blk">
        <h2>The cookie table</h2>
        <p>POL-54 requires this page to carry a table of every cookie the site sets, built from an
          actual scan rather than from memory. The scan returns nothing, so the table is empty.</p>
        <p class="tablenote">No cookies or similar technologies are set by this website.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="blk">
        <h2>If that changes</h2>
        <p>Adding an online booking tool, an embedded map, a video, a chat widget or a social media
          feed can each bring storage and consent obligations with it. We check what a new service
          sets before we add it, not afterwards. If we ever add something that needs your consent,
          we will ask before it is set, refusing will be exactly as easy as accepting, and this page
          and its table will be updated at the same time — not later.</p>
        <p>The site is scanned before launch and at least annually after it.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="blk">
        <h2>Your browser</h2>
        <p>You can block or delete cookies in your browser settings whatever any website says. On
          this site there is nothing for those settings to act on.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="blk">
        <h2>Questions and complaints</h2>
        <p>Ask us about anything on this page, or tell us if you think it is wrong:
          {' '}<a href={`mailto:${site.contact.email}`}>{site.contact.email}</a>. How we handle
          information about you is set out in our <a href="/privacy">privacy notice</a>, and a
          complaint about this page is handled under our
          {' '}<a href="/complaints">complaints procedure</a>.</p>
        <p>You can also complain to the <a href={p.ico.url} rel="noopener">{p.ico.name}</a> at any
          time. Our ICO registration number is {p.ico.registration}.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .narrow{max-width:72ch}
  .blk{padding:34px 0;border-top:1px solid var(--line)}
  .blk:first-of-type{border-top:0;padding-top:0}
  .prose a{color:var(--gold-dim)}
  .warnbar{margin-bottom:30px}
  /* La tabla vacía se publica como una afirmación, no como un hueco: un
     espacio en blanco donde se espera una tabla se lee como un descuido. */
  .tablenote{border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:12px;background:var(--paper);
             padding:22px 24px;font-family:var(--mono);font-size:13.5px;color:var(--ink-soft);
             max-width:none;margin-top:20px}
</style>
